.omo/plans/world-model-data-pipeline.md:98:  What to do / Must NOT do: Implement `world_model/data/dataset.py` as a PyTorch `Dataset` over an `EpisodeCatalog` snapshot. A `TemporalWindowRequest(prediction_steps, stride_frames)` has positive integers and derives `horizon_frames = prediction_steps * stride_frames`; materialize a deterministic index of eligible `(episode, accepted-shot, start-frame)` candidates, but decode PNGs only inside `__getitem__`. Return a documented dictionary with `context_image`, ordered `target_images` at offsets `stride_frames, ..., prediction_steps * stride_frames`, one strict `[5]` per-shot `action`, `frame_indices`, derived `horizon_frames`, `prediction_steps`, `stride_frames`, and immutable provenance (`split`, source-level key or `None`, episode, shot, capture-contract descriptor, declared capabilities, and validated relative sidecar paths). Convert PNGs to RGB tensors with an explicit callable transform; default to lossless `[0,1]` channel-first conversion without resize/normalization. Reject a request with no eligible contiguous window; if a cataloged file disappears before decode, raise a typed read error rather than rescan, bridge shots, or fabricate targets. Do not open, parse, tensorize, pad, or use physics sidecars in a curriculum/ablation during this plan.
